wh40k-footfall-market-guide-intro = Welcome to the Footfall exchange. Edric Moss. I help cargo find buyers and owners avoid selling their boots with it.
wh40k-footfall-market-guide-menu = Where shall we start: receiving pads, appraisal, or payment?
wh40k-footfall-market-guide-start-question = How do I sell cargo?
wh40k-footfall-market-guide-start-answer = Put the goods on a sale pad near a terminal. Its clerk counts the pads in its service area; something still in your hand is not offered for sale. Crates go with their contents, so remove personal belongings first.
wh40k-footfall-market-guide-appraise-question = Checking prices first.
wh40k-footfall-market-guide-appraise-answer = Open the terminal and choose Appraise. It shows the value and number of accepted entries. Appraisal sells nothing. If you move the cargo, request a new one; the exchange cannot read your intentions.
wh40k-footfall-market-guide-confirm-question = Confirming a sale.
wh40k-footfall-market-guide-confirm-answer = Sell transfers all accepted cargo on the served pads to the buyer. You cannot call it back from this side of the counter. Check crates and nearby receiving spots: the terminal does not distinguish your parcel from your neighbour's.
wh40k-footfall-market-guide-payment-question = Where does payout go?
wh40k-footfall-market-guide-payment-answer = Payment is in cash: credits are issued beside the terminal. Collect them after selling. They do not deposit themselves into your account; use a banking terminal. Our shopkeepers charge your account, so that step is useful.
wh40k-footfall-market-guide-missing-question = Unaccepted goods.
wh40k-footfall-market-guide-missing-answer = Check that the goods are on a sale pad near a working terminal. Anchored goods, items with no appraisal value and excluded cargo stay with you. A zero appraisal is a reason to check the cargo, not to keep pressing Sell.
wh40k-footfall-market-guide-farewell = Good trading. Count your boots before leaving; the exchange appreciates care.
wh40k-footfall-market-marker-desc = Persistent source for a protected NPC. Rotate the arrow for facing and place the source manually. A seated actor needs a free bench or chair on its tile.
